From b4d69a318a531a06a4e4446393365a544668ae8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:19:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban overlap: one isolated negative per
 same-creator / re-issue / dup-detector guard

PR #2329's post-merge mutant run (card t_01a1d5e5bf3ccad9, sdlc-review scripts/mutants.py at
origin/main fb2398dd9b) left 12 of 24 exact-anchor mutants alive: 41 tests passed under each.
The re-issue guards were each redundant because the only negative case (t_01a1d4e145f389a5,
2 h later, another run) fails several of them at once, so dropping any one would turn a
refusal into a silent reuse of the first card.

Test-only. Each new test starts from one passing case and changes exactly one input:
- A12 has_key, A13 created_at before the run, A17 a non-local (replica) row: refused, not
  deduplicated (one parametrized case each).
- A14 a reworded title scoring under REISSUE_SCORE: refused.
- A15 a shared-code-only match with a perfect short-title score: refused, not deduplicated.
- A9 shared identifiers but unrelated titles (score < IDS_SCORE): no match.
- A3 the in-transaction re-check (shared_code=False) skips the shared-code rule.
- A16 a shared-code match the new card cites by id is admitted.
- A2 an own card carrying the worker's own chat session is still compared; another creator
  in that session keeps the exemption.
- A6 a review and its implement card from one creator are admitted.
- A21 through kanban_create with no assignee argument: the check judges the resolved
  profile, so a same-title card for another assignee is created.
- A19 the same card noted three times by the dup detector adds one comment.

Proof (same spec rebuilt from the card's list; the worker-3 copy was unreachable):
mutants.py on the 2 original + 2 new files: baseline 54 passed; tally killed 12, each by
exactly one new test. The new files also pass on PR #2481's head f46f3695fd (81 passed with
the original files), so they do not depend on its guard changes.

Note (not fixed here): the detector dedupes a repeat only against comments, so the card
whose occurrence is in the detector card's body adds one duplicate comment line if it
completes again. At most one extra line; left as is.
